==English==
{{wikipedia|mojo (African-American culture)}}

===Etymology 1===
Probably of Creole origin, cognate with [[Gullah]] {{m|gul|moco||witchcraft}}, [[Fula]] {{m|ff|moco'o||medicine man}}. The origin of the drug sense is uncertain, possibly related to {{cog|es|mojar|t=to toast (celebrate with a drink)}}.<ref>{{R:OED2|id=00149595|entry=mojo<sup>2</sup>}}</ref>

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmoʊd͡ʒoʊ/|a=GenAm}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈməʊd͡ʒəʊ/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-mojo.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|əʊdʒəʊ|s=2}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~|s|mojoes}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[magic]] [[spell]] or [[hex]].
# {{lb|en|countable}} An [[object]] (such as a [[charm]] or [[amulet]]) used to [[cast]] [[magic]] [[spell]]s, especially in [[hoodoo]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1991|month=July/August|author=w:Shelby Foote|title=When Robert Johnson Sings|journal={{w|American Heritage (magazine)|American Heritage}}|volume=42|issue=4|url=https://www.americanheritage.com/when-robert-johnson-sings|passage=A doney, for instance, is a woman of worse than doubtful morals, and a nation sack is a cloth pouch worn on a string around the neck for holding '''mojos''' and small change.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} [[spellcraft|Spellcraft]], [[hoodoo]].
# {{lb|en|informal}} [[supernatural|Supernatural]] [[skill]]; [[exceptional]] [[luck]], [[success]]{{,}} or [[power]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022-02-12|author=Danny Westneat|title=The reason voters see past the terrible headlines with Seattle schools|journal=w:The Seattle Times|url=https://www.seattletimes.com/seattle-news/heres-a-story-seattle-schools-actually-did-all-right-during-the-pandemic/|passage=I haven’t seen much '''mojo''' in the state Legislature for that or any other major intervention, though. Hey, lawmakers, you should check out the test scores for your own school districts. It might be yours are needing some help, too, maybe even more so than Seattle.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} Personal [[magnetism]]; [[charm]].
# {{lb|en|slang}} [[sex appeal|Sex appeal]]; [[sex drive]].
#: {{ux|en|Look at the way the chicks are checking out Daniel on the dancefloor. He's still got plenty of '''mojo'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|After the pandemic closed down the discos, I stopped socializing and have lost my '''mojo'''.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} An [[illegal]] [[drug]], especially [[morphine]] or other [[narcotic]]s.
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:recreational drug}}
# {{lb|en|slang|usually with "wire"}} A [[telecopier]]; a [[fax machine]].

===Verb===
{{en-verb|pres=mojoes}}

# {{lb|en|informal|transitive}} To [[cast]] a [[magic]] [[spell]] or [[jinx]] a [[person]].
# {{lb|en|informal|transitive}} To [[annoy]] or [[bother]] someone. 

